  "_comment": "Known Hebrew (BHS/Masoretic) vs. English (KJV-tradition) chapter/verse numbering divergences, for the OT (canon_id 1-39). Keyed by \"canon_id:hebChapter\" — canon_id here means Scheme A per CLAUDE.md's 'book_id means two different things' note (stable 1-39 for OT, Genesis=1..Malachi=39), the SAME numbering tokens_bhs.book_id, resolveChapter()'s bookId, and VERSIFICATION_MAP already use — NOT the site's interspersed book-menu position numbers. Each entry is a list of verse-range correspondences for that Hebrew chapter; a single Hebrew chapter can span parts of two different English chapters (e.g. Numbers 17). Malachi (39) and Joel (29) are intentionally excluded — they're already special-cased in server.js's VERSIFICATION_MAP/DISPLAY_LAST_CHAPTER to DISPLAY English chapter numbers directly, so there's no divergence left to note about for those two. Psalms (19) are intentionally excluded — the offset there is systematic (most psalm titles count as verse 1 in Hebrew) and needs verification against which superscriptions this corpus's own tokens_bhs actually stores as verse 1 before any mapping can be trusted; flagged as follow-up work, not guessed at here. Source: standard, well-established Hebrew/English versification-difference table (matthewbarron.org's versification comparison, following the standard scholarly/SWORD-project convention). Spot-checked live against bldbible.com vs. biblehub.com for Deuteronomy 13 (2026-08-18) before this file was written; a few more entries should be spot-checked the same way before this is fully trusted (see verify step in the implementation).",
